# Verify Transaction

Confirm the status of a transaction using the transaction reference. This is a critical step in your integration to verify payment completion before fulfilling orders or granting access to digital services.

{% endpoint method="GET" path="/transaction/verify/:reference" /%}

{% callout type="info" title="Authentication Required" %}
All requests to the Paystack API require authorization via your secret key. Include your key in the HTTP Header as `Authorization: Bearer YOUR_SECRET_KEY`.
{% /callout %}

{% callout type="tip" title="Interactive API Console" %}
Use the sticky API Explorer console on the right panel to test live transaction verification with any reference (e.g., `7PV9766bsq`) and your test secret key.
{% /callout %}

---

## Path Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `reference` | `string` | **Required** | The transaction reference to verify (e.g. `7PV9766bsq`). |

---

## Integration Code Example

Here is how you verify a transaction using Node.js:

```javascript
const paystack = require('paystack')('sk_test_YOUR_SECRET_KEY');

paystack.transaction.verify('7PV9766bsq')
  .then((response) => {
    if (response.data.status === 'success') {
      console.log('Payment successful! Amount:', response.data.amount / 100);
    } else {
      console.log('Payment pending or failed:', response.data.gateway_response);
    }
  })
  .catch((error) => {
    console.error('Verification error:', error);
  });
```

---

## Response Reference

### `200 OK` (Verification Successful)

When a transaction status is queried, Paystack returns a `200 OK` status with the complete payment payload and authorization metadata:

```json
{
  "status": true,
  "message": "Verification successful",
  "data": {
    "id": 200994508,
    "domain": "test",
    "status": "success",
    "reference": "7PV9766bsq",
    "amount": 20000,
    "message": null,
    "gateway_response": "Successful",
    "paid_at": "2026-08-22T20:20:10.000Z",
    "created_at": "2026-08-22T20:20:00.000Z",
    "channel": "card",
    "currency": "NGN",
    "ip_address": "41.203.76.60",
    "metadata": "",
    "customer": {
      "id": 84315482,
      "first_name": null,
      "last_name": null,
      "email": "customer@example.com",
      "customer_code": "CUS_xn7gfr1n1a1d7lb",
      "phone": null,
      "metadata": null,
      "risk_action": "default"
    },
    "authorization": {
      "authorization_code": "AUTH_8sm2h0z9w1",
      "bin": "408408",
      "last4": "4081",
      "exp_month": "12",
      "exp_year": "2030",
      "channel": "card",
      "card_type": "visa",
      "bank": "TEST BANK",
      "country_code": "NG",
      "brand": "visa",
      "reusable": true,
      "signature": "SIG_y37w2903v"
    }
  }
}
```

{% callout type="important" title="Best Practice: Verify Amount & Currency" %}
Always check that `data.status === "success"` and verify that `data.amount` matches the expected order total before releasing value to the customer.
{% /callout %}
